config.description:
Source-specific parameters. Examples:
  incubator → {incubator_name: "Y Combinator", batch_id: "W25", target_title_tags: ["founder", "ceo"]}
  linkedin_post_reactors → {query: "<post URL or keyword>", interaction_types: ["like","comment"]}
  job_posting → {job_title_tags: ["AE","SDR"], location_tags: ["US"], days: 30}
  targeted_search → {job_title_tags: [...], location_tags: [...], company_linkedin_urls: [...]}
Missing fields get sensible defaults the user can edit in the visual builder.

Partial config patch to merge into the current ingress config. Keys not provided are preserved. Pass `source_kind` to swap the ingress to a different kind (e.g. "manual" for CSV Import) — when swapping, only include fields valid for the new kind; previously-merged keys incompatible with the new schema will be dropped by the backend. Examples:
  {"job_title_tags": ["Founding AE","Founding SDR"]}
  {"batch_id": "W26"}
  {"keyword_tags": ["SaaStr 2026"], "from_date": "2026-05-01"}
  {"interaction_types": ["like"]}
  {"source_kind": "manual"}  (swap to CSV Import)
